  "description": "01 s3: the canonical key of a merged group is its lexicographically smallest MEMBER key, and every key a merge decision names is a member - including a key no posting has any more (a stale decision, e.g. after a source was deleted). 'ardent hollow' has no posting: merging it with 'birch hollow' and 'cedar hollow' makes it the group's key (and company_id), although it is not among the present keys. 'zenith row' is absent too, but larger than both present keys, so the group of 'dune row' and 'elm row' that it joins keeps 'dune row'; the merge is transitive through an absent key either way. Two roles dedupe across the merged companies (same title and location, two sources).",
